# cloudflared environment — the public-edge tunnel token (WI-101). One of
# TWO secrets files in this stack (the other is dart_services.env).
#
# Copy to deploy/env/cloudflared.env and fill in ON THE EVENT HOST.
# deploy/env/*.env is gitignored (deploy/env/.gitignore) — never commit it.
#
# Get the token from the Cloudflare Zero Trust dashboard:
#   Networks → Tunnels → Create tunnel → cloudflared → name it →
#   the "install connector" step shows a token (the long string after
#   `cloudflared ... run --token`). Copy JUST the token value here.
#
# The tunnel's Public Hostnames (set in the same dashboard) must be:
#   flutterinthedark.dev         →  http://traefik:80
#   backend.flutterinthedark.dev →  http://traefik:80
# (the dashboard auto-creates the proxied CNAMEs — NO A records to the
# house IP).
#
# Verify blind, never print values (W-083/W-149):
#   [ -f deploy/env/cloudflared.env ] && echo exists
#   grep -q '^TUNNEL_TOKEN=' deploy/env/cloudflared.env && echo key-present
#   chmod 600 deploy/env/cloudflared.env

# REQUIRED — the tunnel token from the dashboard. cloudflared reads
# TUNNEL_TOKEN automatically when running `tunnel run` (token-only mode,
# no credentials JSON, no committed config file — the ingress map lives in
# the dashboard).
TUNNEL_TOKEN=
